          %h2#introduction Introduction
          %p
            The goal of this article is to prove that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+space"} compact Hausdorff
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+space"} profinite
            ring, i.e., is canonically isomorphic as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+ring"} topological ring
            to its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+completion"} profinite completion
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi R
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{R}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
            rings with their
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+topology"} discrete topologies
          %p
            Further commentary on this result can be found in a Café
            %a{:href => "#Lein"} blog post
            of Tom Leinster, in connection with some work by his student Barry Devlin.
          %h2#preliminaries Preliminaries
          %p
            All topological rings considered are
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+axiom"} separation axiom
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+structures"} uniform structures
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff
            and even
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tychonoff+spaces"} Tychonoff spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a finite ring and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: R \to S
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous
            ring homomorphism, this means the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            must be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+set"} open
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            (for us, “ideal” always means two-sided ideal), since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0\}
            is open in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            In the converse direction, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a compact ring and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            is an open ideal, then the ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R/I
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+topology"} quotient topology
            coming from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is discrete (every point is open), and compact since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is compact, and so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R/I
            must then be finite.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(R)
            denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            of open ideals of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} inclusion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+set"} codirected
            by taking finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
            of ideals. Each inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \subseteq J
            induces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjection
            of finite rings
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R/I \to R/J
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ring
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(R) \to Ring
            whose (projective)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            is the profinite completion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi R
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{R}
            of
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi proj
                    %mi I
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} proj_I: R \to R/I
            of course induce a canonical map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo :
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi R
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi: R \to \widehat{R}
          #surj.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo :
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi R
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi: R \to \widehat{R}
              is surjective.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is compact and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi R
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{R}
              is Hausdorff, the image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi(R)
              is closed in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi R
                        %mo ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{R}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subspace"} dense subspace
            %p
              So, we are to show that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mover
                      %mi R
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subseteq \widehat{R}
              is open and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in R
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi(x) \in U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi I
                    %mo :
                    %mover
                      %mi R
                      %mo ^
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_I: \widehat{R} \to R/I
              denote a typical component map of the limit cone. A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis+of+a+topology"} basis
              for the topology of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi R
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{R}
              consists of inhabited finite intersections of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi …
                    %mo ∩
                    %msubsup
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = \pi_{I_1}^{-1}(x_1) \cap \ldots \cap \pi_{I_n}^{-1}(x_n)
              where each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_k
              is a point of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R/I_k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is of this form.
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mover
                      %mi R
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y = \langle y_I \rangle_{I \in \mathcal{O}(R)} \in \widehat{R}
              be any point belonging to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              (so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y_{I_i} = x_i
              for
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i = 1, \ldots, n
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                      %mo =
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J = \bigcap_{i=1}^n I_i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i
              the coordinate
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y_J
              maps to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i
              under the map
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi J
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R/J \to R/I_i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y' \in R
              be an element that maps to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y_J
              under
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \to R/J
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi(y')
              lies in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              and we are done.
          %h2#compact_rings_are_totally_disconnected Compact rings are totally disconnected
          %p
            A key technical result is the following (see this
            = succeed "-Category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#Trim"} comment
          #totdisc.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Every compact Hausdorff ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+space"} totally disconnected
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^\ast
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin+duality"} Pontryagin dual
              of (the additive group of)
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^\ast
              is discrete. As
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^\ast
              are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+Hausdorff+space"} locally compact Hausdorff
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponentiable+space"} exponentiable
              as spaces, and it follows quickly that the functorial maps
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(R, R) \to Hom(R^\ast, R^\ast), \qquad Hom(R^\ast, R^\ast) \to Hom(R^{\ast\ast}, R^{\ast\ast}) \cong Hom(R, R)
            %p
              are continuous homomorphisms of topological groups. Using naturality of the isomorphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ≅
                      %msup
                        %mi R
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \cong R^{\ast\ast}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              of topological groups.
            %p
              The multiplication map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ×
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \times R \to R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/currying"} transforms
              to a continuous injection
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi R
                      %mo →
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo ,
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi R
                        %mo *
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi R
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: R \to Hom(R, R) \cong Hom(R^\ast, R^\ast)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is compact and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(R^\ast, R^\ast)
              is Hausdorff, the injection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              homeomorphically onto its image in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi R
                        %mo *
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi R
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(R^\ast, R^\ast)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(R^\ast, R^\ast)
              is manifestly a subspace of a product of discrete spaces and hence totally disconnected, so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is totally disconnected as well. (In more detail: if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \subseteq R
              is connected, then the image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              under the composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi R
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi i
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi R
                          %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo →
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi proj
                          %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \subseteq R \stackrel{i}{\to} Hom(R^\ast, R^\ast) \hookrightarrow \prod_{x \in R^\ast} R^\ast \stackrel{proj_x}{\;\;\to\;\;} R^\ast
            %p
              is also connected and hence a one-point space for each
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi R
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in R^\ast
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i(C)
              and therefore
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              are one-point spaces.)
          %h2#compact_rings_have_enough_open_ideals Compact rings have enough open ideals
          %p
            By Theorem
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#totdisc"}
          #compopen.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a compact Hausdorff totally disconnected space. For each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              and open neighborhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in U \subseteq V
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              In a compact Hausdorff space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+space#connected_components"} connected component
              of a point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              equals its quasi-component; an online proof may be found
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://math.stackexchange.com/a/11423/43208"} here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is also totally disconnected, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is also the intersection of all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/clopen+set"} clopens
              containing it. Now let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              be an open
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighborhood"} neighborhood
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi K
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi clopen
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcap_{x \in K\; clopen} K \subseteq V
              and therefore
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi V
                      %mo ⊆
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi K
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi clopen
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg V \subseteq \bigcup_{x \in K\; clopen} \neg K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg V
              is compact, finitely many such clopens
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ¬
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg K_1, \ldots, \neg K_n
              cover
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg V
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ≔
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mi K
                        %mi n
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \coloneqq \bigcap_{i=1}^n K_n \subseteq V
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is compact and open and contains
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
          #opengroup.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              be a compact Hausdorff totally disconnected abelian group. For each open neighborhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \in A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi O
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O \subseteq V
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              By Lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#compopen"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi W
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \in W \subseteq V
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %mi W
                    %mo ×
                    %mi W
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha: W \times W \to A
              be the restriction of the addition operation
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} +: A \times A \to A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              is continuous, there is for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in W
              an open neighborhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msup
                      %mi α
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_x \times U_x \subseteq \alpha^{-1}(W)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x, 0)
              where we may assume
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x
              is
              %em symmetric
              (i.e.,
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x = -U_x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_x
              cover
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{x_1}, \ldots, V_{x_n}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 1
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi …
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = U_{x_1} \cap \ldots \cap U_{x_n}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi W
                      %mo ×
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha(W \times U) \subseteq W
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo +
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W + U \subseteq W
              for short. This
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is again symmetric:
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = -U
            %p
              Hence if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mi U
                    %mo +
                    %mi …
                    %mo +
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^n = U + \ldots + U
              denotes the set of all sums of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              elements belonging to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^n
              is open and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W + U^n \subseteq W
              by induction, whence
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi U
                        %mi n
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^n \subseteq W
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is symmetric, the union
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O = \bigcup_n U^n
              is the subgroup generated by
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              and therefore also in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          #openideal.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_3 Lemma
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be a compact Hausdorff totally disconnected ring. For each open neighborhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \subseteq V
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              By Lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#opengroup"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi O
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O \subseteq V
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi R
                      %mo :
                      %mi R
                      %mi x
                      %mi R
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = \{x \in R: R x R \subseteq O\}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \in I
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              is an ideal of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in I
              fixed. For each
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi R
                      %mo ×
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a, b) \in R \times R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_{(a, b)}
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_{(a, b)}'
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{(a, b)}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi O
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_{(a, b)} V_{(a, b)} W_{(a, b)}' \subseteq O
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ×
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \times R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_{(a, b)} \times W_{(a, b)}'
              cover
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ×
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \times R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcap_{i=1}^n V_{(a_i, b_i)}
              is an open neighborhood of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              that is contained in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
          %h2#compact_rings_are_profinite Compact rings are profinite
          %p Now for our final result.
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              a compact ring, the canonical map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo :
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi R
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi: R \to \widehat{R}
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} injective
          %p
            This and Proposition
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#surj"}
            taken together imply that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            is a ring isomorphism. It is also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
            because it is a continuous
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijective
            map from a compact space to a Hausdorff space. Therefore
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            is an isomorphism of topological rings.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_6 Proof
            %p
              As we have an inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi R
                      %mo ^
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{R} \hookrightarrow \prod_{I \in \mathcal{O}(R)} R/I
              of the profinite completion as projective limit, we see the kernel of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
              is the same as the kernel of
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi proj
                      %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle proj_I \rangle_{I \in \mathcal{O}(R)}: R \to \prod_{I \in \mathcal{O}(R)} R/I
            %p
              which is precisely
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                        %mrow
                          %mi I
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcap_{I \in \mathcal{O}(R)} I
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#openideal"}
              every neighborhood of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \in R
              contains an open ideal
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \in \mathcal{O}(R)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0\}
              since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is Hausdorff. Thus the kernel of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
              is trivial, as was to be shown.
